<title>USA: TABLE - Halifax Corp Q1 loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Halifax Corp Q1 loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>ALEXANDRIA, Va. 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>FIRST QUARTER ENDED JUNE 30,		1997	     1996</p>
<p> Revenues				  $18,035,000    $15,640,000</p>
<p> Income before income taxes	    (384,000)	  435,000</p>
<p> Income taxes				(152,000)	  166,000</p>
<p> Net income (loss)			 (232,000)	  269,000</p>
<p>Net income (loss) per common and</p>
<p>common equivalent shares</p>
<p>    -- primary				  (0.11)	     0.13</p>
<p>    -- fully diluted			  (0.11)	     0.13</p>
<p>Weighted average number of</p>
<p>common shares outstanding</p>
<p>    -- primary			     2,041,891	2,014,640</p>
<p>    -- fully diluted		     2,041,891	2,026,211</p>
<p>The net income per common share reported in the 6/30/96 quarter has been restated for the dilutive effect of common equivalent shares on a basis consistent with the 6/30/97 quarter, resulting in dilution of $0.01 from the originally reported $0.14 (adjusted for 3:2 stock split) for both primary and fully diluted net income per share.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
